\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar jumps to 1-week high as euro loses momentum.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2003\par 07:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The dollar swept to a one-week high versus the euro and firmed against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, helped by Wall Street's latest rally.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's rise against the euro started on Monday after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said a Group of Seven (G7) call last month for exchange rate flexibility was not directed at the euro.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 issued a statement in September calling for more flexibility in exchange rates. That was widely perceived in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as a demand that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and China stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of their export markets.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said Duisenberg's comments provided traders an opportunity to adjust positions.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think what Duisenberg said was anything new. The market's position was tilted towards the euro and so I think the fall was an adjustment," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the euro rose to within one cent of its record high of $1.1932 hit earlier in the year. Many traders think euro long positions had accumulated to the extent that an adjustment was inevitable.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday morning the euro fell more than a full U.S. cent to a one-week low of $1.1606 versus 1.1712/16 in late U.S. trade Monday, when it also fell nearly one percent.  \par \par \uc2 As of 0302 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.1621/26 .  \par \par \uc2 It slipped to around 126.83 yen compared with 127.45.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback also rose to 109.36 yen , about a quarter of a percent above 108.90/00 in late U.S. trade, and more than one yen above a three-year low of 108.28 yen on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar also rose to a one-week high against the Swiss franc around\par 1.3320 franc  and also against the Australian dollar       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "New York shares were also strong, and that prompted an adjustment of recent excessive weakness in the dollar," said Seiya Nakajima, chief economist at Itochu Corp.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Nasdaq Composite Index on Monday jumped to its highest close in more than 20 months after surprisingly rosy results from mobile phone maker Motorola Inc (MOT.N) boosted investors' hopes for strong third-quarter earnings.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The blue-chip Dow Jones Industrial Average posted its highest close since June, 2002.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FOCUS ON BUSH VISIT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the yen, the dollar was also helped by wariness about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's export-hurting appreciation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But traders noted uncertainty about Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy ahead of Bush's visit to Japan on Friday. Bush is expected to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when he meets Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If Bush preaches the virtues of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility, that would be taken as indirect criticism against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and would lift the yen against the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the other hand, Bush may say he believes in a strong dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That would be a shot in the arm for Tokyo's efforts to curb the yen's strength and traders think Bush may make such comments possibly in exchange for a sizable donation - possibly in the billions of dollars - from Japan to help rebuild Iraq.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In general, market players are well prepared for a further rise in the yen," said Takashi Toyahara, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Nomura Securities. "So, if there is to be a surprise, it will be a rise in the dollar," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031014dzae000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
