\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar holds near three-year lows vs yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2003\par 04:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Oct 13 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted just above\par three-year lows against the yen in quiet trade on Monday, with\par activity limited due to holidays in Japan and the United\par States.\par     The dollar sank to a fresh three-year low on Friday after\par the Bank of Japan (BOJ) unexpectedly boosted the amount of\par money in the financial system by raising the upper end of its\par target for banks' current accounts held at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar has fallen six percent against the yen since a\par meeting of top industrialised nations in late September called\par for more flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regimes.\par  \par     This was seen by the market as a signal to sell the dollar\par and buy euros and Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "I'm still going to be cautious on dollar-yen because there\par is a lot of downwards momentum there," said Jan Lambregts, head\par of Asia-Pacific research at Rabobank, Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The best we can hope for this week is stabilisation which\par might be seen by the BOJ as a moment to step in and push\par dollar-yen higher."\par     The dollar was quoted at 108.36 yen        in Asian morning\par trade, compared with 108.60 yen in late New York on Friday and\par a new three-year low of 108.28 yen.\par     The euro stood at $1.1800       , barely changed from New\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par York's late $1.1801, and at 127.95 yen  against\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 128.13. The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still more than a cent off a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lifetime high of 1.1932 seen on May 27. The euro was first\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traded in January 1999.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's surprise move last week was seen by some in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market as both an attempt to counter yen strength and to spur\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the world's second-biggest economy, but its impact may be\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The history of BOJ action on this is that it's had zero\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact on the yen," said Michael Jansen, strategist at National\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Australia Bank in Sydney.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's not making a material difference to dollar/yen\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because it's more of a U.S. dollar story anyway... The only\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact the BOJ is going to have on the yen is through direct\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but then it's negating that by going out and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sterilising the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plays."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Sunday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reiterated his view that the main purpose of Tokyo's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     This view is seen by markets as implying Tokyo may accept\par that the yen may rise further in coming months.\par     LOW VOLUME\par     Volume is seen remaining low today because of the Columbus\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Day holiday in the United States, with government offices,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks and fixed-income markets closed, and because Japan is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shut for the Health Sports Day holiday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One-month options volatility in the euro/dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is holding near one-year highs, a sign that traders expect the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "It's very quiet. It has literally been in a 10-point range\par today," said one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader in Singapore.\par     "But it can be interpreted as being bearish for dollar-yen\par because we are languishing 15 points off the three-year lows\par and there's no bounce at all," he added.\par     The market is awaiting a rash of U.S. economic data later\par this week for fresh direction.\par     The Federal Reserve's Beige Book, an anecdotal narrative\par describing business conditions around the nation, is due on\par Wednesday and may offer a more upbeat view of the economy.\par     September retail sales numbers are expected to retreat from\par August levels.\par     Economists polled by Reuters estimated that retail sales\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slipped 0.1 percent in September after rising 0.6 percent in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par August, but that sales excluding autos rose 0.4 percent, on top\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of August's 0.7 percent increase.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Those two are the big risk events. Otherwise the dollar is\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technically oversold but nobody out there is happy to go and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buy at these levels, mainly because there is a significant\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chance of further downside in dollar/yen," National Australia's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jansen said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "No one is a buyer of last resort for the U.S. dollar right\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031013dzad000uo\par }\page {\par\fs2