\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar down vs yen following BoJ ease.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 22:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The dollar tumbled broadly on Friday, touching a fresh three-year low against the yen after markets perceived the latest Bank of Japan monetary easing as a pro-growth measure that could spur the world's second-biggest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback's decline followed a broad-based dollar rally on Thursday that was triggered by positive U.S. jobs data. Dollar sentiment was turning bearish again on Friday amid a growing perception that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to weaken to help finance the ballooning U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The BoJ easing helped trigger a sell-off in the dollar to a new three-year low against the yen as traders read between the lines that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was bracing for continued yen strength with a defensive measure.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar dropped 0.43 percent to 108.60 yen , after falling to a new three-year low of 108.28 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It does raise suspicion that the Bank of Japan is pretty much resigned to yen appreciation and is looking ahead to a crimp in exports," said Sean Callow, IDEAglobal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst.  \par \par \uc2 In late New York trade, the euro climbed 0.50 percent to $1.1801 . The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose 0.17 percent against the yen to 128.13 yen .  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3115 francs , down 0.34 percent on the day. The pound fell 0.19 percent against the dollar to $1.6632 .  \par \par \uc2 "There's a speculative frost out there. Thematically, it is a continuation of the dollar's downtrend," said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast Inc in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the dollar's rally on Thursday after a drop in weekly U.S. jobless claims served to clear out short positions on the greenback, specifically against the euro, suggesting further weakness in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Next week, traders will watch for reports on U.S. retail sales and consumer prices.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ SURPRISE EASING  \par \par \uc2 The story of the day was the BoJ's surprise easing overnight. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly raised the upper end of its target for banking system liquidity and made its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible.  \par \par \uc2 BoJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui said the easing was intended to underpin a nascent economic recovery, and Tokyo's Nikkei average responded positively, ending up 2.42 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Aiming to boost excess liquidity in the banking system, the BoJ said it would raise the upper end of its target range for current account deposits that banks keep at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 32 trillion yen ($293 billion) from 30 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 "The easing is helpful but it would just be on the margin. I don't think the measure would make a difference in stemming the yen's appreciation," said 4Cast's Ruskin.  \par \par \uc2 Other analysts said the yen's advance in the face of easing suggests the market is not taking the BoJ seriously.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems to be a loss of credibility on the part of the BoJ," said Lauren Germain, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banc of America Securities in New York. "We continue to think that it becomes harder to defend any line-in-the-sand figure."  \par \par \uc2 Traders were alert to signs of possible BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although some analysts believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step aside ahead of U.S. President George W. Bush's visit to Tokyo next week.  \par \par \uc2 US TRADE, PPI DATA  \par \par \uc2 The dollar gained a modest, fleeting bid against the euro after the U.S. trade deficit narrowed in August to $39.2 billion, down from a revised tally of $40 billion in July.  \par \par \uc2 "The trade numbers are better both in real and nominal terms. It tells you that trade won't be a drag in the third quarter," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Merrill Lynch in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The September U.S. producer price index rose at a faster-than-expected pace of 0.3 percent, compared with a rise of 0.4 percent in August.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031010dzaa003jc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
