\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Japan policy easing seen no worry for yen bulls.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn   \par \uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 17:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan's unexpected decision to ease monetary policy on Friday will do little to stop the yen from soaring because upbeat sentiment over a Japanese recovery has already taken hold, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 Japan, which already has interest rates practically at zero, raised the ceiling for liquidity it provides to the banking sector in order to encourage banks to lend and invest to get the economy moving faster.   \par \par \uc2 By increasing the amount of money sloshing around in the economy, the move raises the amount of yen in circulation and a knock-on effect might be to help dilute its value.   \par \par \uc2 "In theory, you would expect monetary easing to weaken a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but history shows that in Japan this has not followed," said Trevor Dinmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "Four of the last six increases in the Bank of Japan's reserve target have been followed by yen gains on a trade-weighted basis and fundamentals suggest dollar/yen should go lower."   \par \par \uc2 The yen did strengthen after Friday's decision, due to increasing economic optimism now the Bank was pumping more money into the system and reinforcing a recent trend of foreign flows into Japanese assets.   \par \par \uc2 It hit three-year highs beyond 108.50 to the dollar , a rise of 6.5 percent since Group of Seven industrialised nations called last month for flexible exchange rate regimes.   \par \par \uc2 It climbed almost a yen against the euro and hit a one-year high against the British pound.   \par \par \uc2 STERILISATION?   \par \par \uc2 Japanese monetary authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively on the foreign exchanges this year, spending a record 13.5 trillion yen so far to weaken the yen and preserve the country's fragile export-led recovery.   \par \par \uc2 Friday's easing was said by some analysts to allow for more "unsterilised" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which money pumped into the market by yen sales is allowed to remain there, instead of being drained out via money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few days later.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the decision to raise the ceiling for current account deposits that banks keep at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implies the BOJ is allowing more yen it has been selling to remain in circulation than before.   \par \par \uc2 Unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can have more effect in weakening a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than sterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it helps to keep interest rates low and so deter potential investors.   \par \par \uc2 On this occasion though analysts were doubtful that unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be any more successful than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous attempts to halt, or at least to steady, the yen's ascent.   \par \par \uc2 "With interest rates at zero and plenty of excess liquidity sloshing round the system, in a practical sense it does not make much difference whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sterilised or not," analysts at ING in Tokyo wrote in a client note.   \par \par \uc2 WHERE NEXT?   \par \par \uc2 Traders say Japan's official bouts of yen selling now seem to be aimed at smoothing, rather than preventing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise after a G7 communique in September appeared to put pressure on Tokyo to keep out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 Before the G7, 115 yen was seen as the "line in the sand" for Japanese authorities. But afterwards this changed to 110.   \par \par \uc2 That changed again once the dollar fell through 110 yen this week, and U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline keeps accelerating.   \par \par \uc2 "This is such a one-way move - the charts suggest we can get to 101/100 and even 95/90 in a matter of weeks or months, rather than of quarters," said Gerry Celaya, technical analyst at Redtower Research.   \par \par \uc2 If so it will outstrip many people's forecasts for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as shown in a Reuters poll of more than 50 analysts this week who on average saw dollar/yen at 105 at the end of September 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Speculators have been unwinding so-called carry trades, which means they are buying back yen which they previously borrowed at low interest rates to fund positions in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 As the yen keeps rising, these investors are forced to buy more yen to cover their positions, which analysts say explains the speed of recent upmoves.   \par \par \uc2 But, after drifting in and out of recession for the past 10 years, Japan's assets also now appeal.   \par \par \uc2 "I've just been in Tokyo, and I've never known a situation before where all the analysts are optimistic," said Nigel Richardson, global investment strategist at Axa Investment Managers.   \par \par \uc2 "There is structural change in Japan - companies are cutting costs and restructuring, doing all the right things, and this recovery will be sustained."   \par \par \uc2 Mike McNaught-Davis, director on the Japanese equities desk at investment boutique Martin Currie, said the yen's rise was not a cause for concern at the moment although it could easily go higher.   \par \par \uc2 "It could spike to 100 yen and beyond. If it did that we would certainly think about hedging as it would then be looking overbought." (Additional reporting by Christina Fincher).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031010dzaa002u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
