\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar tumbles vs yen on further Japan optimism.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 15:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The dollar sagged against the yen on Friday amid continued speculative pressure as markets expected the latest Bank of Japan monetary easing to further boost the recovery of the world's second-biggest economy.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback was also pounded by other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after rallying on Thursday. Sentiment on the dollar was turning bearish again on a growing perception that it has to weaken to finance the ballooning U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "The focus of the market is to continue to sell the dollar," said Marc Chandler, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC in New York. "The dollar's bounces have been (increasingly) shorter in duration and shallower in amplitude," he said.  \par \par \uc2 In early New York trade, the euro climbed 0.70 percent to $1.1825. The single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose a quarter of a percent against a resurgent yen to 128.21 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3092 francs, down 0.52 percent on the day. The pound edged higher to $1.6678.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ SURPRISE EASING  \par \par \uc2 But the story of the day was the BoJ's surprise easing overnight. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly raised the upper end of its target for banking system liquidity and made its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible.  \par \par \uc2 "The move suggests they are aware of the effect on the economy from the yen appreciation. In an economy grappling with a liquidity trap, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and half-hearted unsterilization is a way of boosting liquidity," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland.  \par \par \uc2 BoJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui said the easing was intended to underpin a nascent economic recovery and Tokyo's Nikkei average responded positively, ending up 2.42 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Aiming to boost excess liquidity in the banking system, the BoJ said it would raise the upper end of its target range for current account deposits that banks keep at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 32 trillion yen ($293 billion) from 30 trillion yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.60 percent to 108.44 yen, after falling to a new three-year low of 108.28 yen. Traders continued to be wary for signs of possible BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although some analysts believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step aside ahead of U.S. President George W. Bush's visit to Tokyo next week.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar/yen is still a one-way bet and that is still dollar weakness. The market completely shrugged off the BoJ's move," said Chandler.  \par \par \uc2 Other analysts said the yen's advance in the face of monetary easing suggests the market is not taking the BoJ seriously.  \par \par \uc2 "There seems to be a loss of credibility on the part of the BoJ," said Lauren Germain, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banc of America Securities in New York. "We continue to think that it becomes harder to defend any line in the sand figure," she added.  \par \par \uc2 US TRADE, PPI DATA  \par \par \uc2 The dollar gained a modest, fleeting bid against the euro after the U.S. trade deficit narrowed unexpectedly in August to $39.2 billion, down from a revised tally of $40 billion in July. The consensus forecast had been for the deficit to widen to $41.3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "The trade numbers are better both in real and nominal terms. It tells you that trade won't be a drag in the third quarter," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Merrill Lynch in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the September U.S. producer price index rose to a faster-than-expected pace of 0.3 percent, compared to a rise of 0.4 percent in August. (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York and Natsuko Waki in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031010dzaa002na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
