\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INSTANT VIEW-BOJ eases monetary policy.   \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Following are immediate views of economists and analysts to an announcement by the Bank of Japan that it would ease monetary policy by expanding the high end of its reserves target to 32 trillion yen ($293.3 billion).   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also decided to extend to one year the period in which it will buy Japanese government bonds (JGBs) under repurchase agreements - a move it had been considering since its last policy meeting.   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 MAKOTO YAMASHITA, STRATEGIST, UFJ TSUBASA SECURITIES   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think anybody in the market expected this.   \par \par \uc2 "Since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in September, they will need to absorb funds from the money market.   \par \par \uc2 "I think they wanted to avoid short-term interest rates from rising since they will likely need to increase fund-absorbing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The other purpose, of course, was to try to prevent a stronger yen."   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 HIRONAO SHIRAKAWA, CHIEF ECONOMIST, UBS SECURITIES   \par \par \uc2 "Though the size was small, it was surprising that the BOJ decided to raise the target for current account deposits (to 32 trillion yen from 30 trillion).   \par \par \uc2 "It's a positive factor for the equity market because it convinced traders the BOJ will provide even more ample liquidity if the yen appreciates further.   \par \par \uc2 "The measure may not be enough to put a break on yen's appreciation, but it is likely to give a boost to stock prices."   \par \par \uc2 - - - -   \par \par \uc2 KOJI SHIMAMOTO, CHIEF STRATEGIST AND HEAD OF INVESTMENT RESEARCH, BNP PARIBAS   \par \par \uc2 "I think the BOJ is showing its concern about the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (stronger yen) and an uptrend in Japan's long-term interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 "But this is not really a surprise as the BOJ has made similar moves in the past, which is to emphasise its commitment to accommodative monetary policy at the time of economic recovery."   \par \par \uc2 - - - -.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031010dzaa000rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
