\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Govt Bonds End Down Despite BOJ Easing; Stks Strong  \b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2003\par 09:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese government bond prices ended sharply lower Friday, despite a surprise decision by the Bank of Japan to ease monetary policy, as stocks rose firmly, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ board, concluding a two-day policy meeting, surprised market participants by deciding to slightly ease monetary policy. It raised the ceiling on its account balance target by Y2 trillion to a range of Y27 trillion to Y32 trillion, leaving the bottom of the target unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 Few players had expected any easing, after volatility in long-term JGB yields had eased and as share prices have been solid, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the BOJ's move didn't have enough impact to pull the bond market out of negative territory.  \par \par \uc2 Although it was a psychological boost for the market, players doubted the easing would have any direct impact on the JGBs because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't increase its outright purchases of bonds from the current monthly Y1.2 trillion, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Lead September 10-year JGB futures ended 0.40 lower at 137.79, though they popped above 138 immediately after the BOJ's announcement. The yield on the newest 10-year JGBs was seven basis points higher at 1.35%.  \par \par \uc2 "It was the strong shares that prompted JGB selling," said a trader at a major Japanese securities house. "I expect the BOJ's easing will support short- to medium-term JGBs in the near-term."  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average ended at 10786.04, up 2.4% from Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Prices as of 0600 GMT: \par  \par    Tiffe Jun 3-Mos Euroyen Price:       99.875  Up 0.025 \par    SGX Jun 3-Mos Euroyen Price:         99.875  Up 0.025 \par    TSE Dec 10Y JGB Future Price:        137.79  Dn 0.40 \par    SGX Dec 10Y JGB Future Price:        137.72  Dn 0.44 \par    10-Yr 1.6% JGB No. 253 Yield:        1.350%  Up 0.07 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Players viewed the BOJ's easing as showing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to take a step to support the government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy to prevent the yen from strengthening further against the dollar, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Increasing the account balance ceiling makes room for the BOJ to continue its money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the government to keep selling yen, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's move "highlighted the BOJ's weak view of Japan's economy - they seem to think the economy is so weak that they need to do something about the stronger yen," traders said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to sell yen, mainly against the dollar, to stem the yen's gains. Such moves boost the amount of money in the BOJ's account balances, reducing the degree to which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can provide funds through its money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ's latest step will provide funds to those who really need money" by ensuring adequate funds for its money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Seiji Shiraishi, chief market economist at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Because Japan's money market isn't functioning well" under the current zero-rate interest rate environment, market participants who buy yen from the BOJ in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market have little incentive to lend it to others in the money market, although they would if rates were higher, Shiraishi said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because it aims to support market liquidity, short-term money markets welcomed the BOJ easing. Lead June three-month Euroyen futures rose to 99.875, the highest level since Aug. 1.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yen interest rate swaps were unstable around the time of BOJ decision, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rates at the short end of the curve shrank early rises, welcoming the easing. But the long end remained high, reflecting higher JGB yields, they said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two-year swaps were flat at 0.22%, five-year swaps was 2.75 basis points higher at 0.7025%, and 10-year swaps were three basis points up at 1.3650%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Michiyo Seki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; michiyo.seki@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hiroshi Miwa contributed to this report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1037 4153  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020031010dzaa0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
