\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits three-year lows against yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2003\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The dollar slid below 109 yen for the first time in three years on Thursday as a suspected dollar-buying spree by Japan served to slow but not halt the greenback's decline.   \par \par \uc2  The view that U.S. and European policymakers will let the dollar fall to correct the U.S. trade deficit gathered weight after Group of Seven nations called for flexible exchange rates last month, putting the dollar under pressure across the board.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar also fell to its lowest in almost four months against the euro in early European trade, but selling momentum showed signs of slowing after six consecutive weeks of losses.   \par \par \uc2  "Japan doesn't like what is happening but they realise they are fighting a broad-based dollar decline," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Mellon.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which has shed over five percent against the yen since mid-September, slid to 108.88 yen in early European trade before talk of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted it from its lows.   \par \par \uc2  Some analysts speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which threw more than 13 trillion yen at the foreign exchanges in the first nine months of the year, was now more concerned with slowing the yen's rise than halting it.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister Masakazu Hayashi said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had been "extremely rapid" but that Japan was not aiming to maintain a specific exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2  GREEN LIGHT   \par \par \uc2  The euro extended gains to $1.1860, less than a cent away from record highs scaled earlier this year, but had fallen back to $1.1785 by 1200 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  Euro zone policymakers continued to sound relaxed about the euro's recent rise.   \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governing council member Ernst Welteke noted the euro's current rate against the dollar was in line with its long-term average, while fellow member Matti Vanhala said euro strength was not a significant hindrance to euro zone growth.   \par \par \uc2  The remarks tallied with comments by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Wim Duisenberg earlier this week that the huge U.S. current account deficit made a weaker dollar inevitable.   \par \par \uc2  Although Japanese officials were thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars twice on Thursday, their resolve to keep it in check was being tested by a market emboldened by an apparent laissez-faire stance by those overseeing other major economies.   \par \par \uc2  "There is a general consensus that the euro is going to go higher and the ECB is not going to do anything to stop it going higher," said Tim Fox, market strategist at National Australia Bank.   \par \par \uc2  "The market is taking little notice of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2  Figures showing a surprise fall in German unemployment fuelled optimism that recent labour market reforms were having an effect, but analysts said data out of the euro zone was currently having little impact on the foreign exchanges.   \par \par \uc2  BROAD-BASED FALL   \par \par \uc2  The dollar also fell to five-year lows against the Swedish crown, six-year lows against the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar and five-year lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  before paring losses.   \par \par \uc2  Questions about the depth of a U.S. recovery centre on strength in the labour market, and weekly jobless claims at 1230 GMT are forecast to show 393,000 new filings, compared with 399,000 in the previous week.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031009dza90024b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
