\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar spirals lower as Japan fights losing battle.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2003\par 12:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a three-year low against the yen and a four-month low versus the euro on Thursday as investors bet the U.S. and European authorities would let it fall to correct the ballooning U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials stepped up their warnings about rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves but suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to stop the dollar sliding for a fourth consecutive day.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan doesn't like what is happening but they realise they are fighting a broad-based dollar decline and will have to accept a stronger yen," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Mellon Financial Corporation.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. current account deficit is always in the background."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has shed more than five percent against the yen since mid-September, stumbled below 109 yen before paring losses as talk of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  swirled through trading floors.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which threw more than 13 trillion yen at the foreign exchanges in the first nine months of the year, was now more concerned with slowing the yen's rise rather than halting it.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's Vice Finance Minister Masakazu Hayashi said recent moves on the foreign exchanges had been "extremely rapid" but that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not aimed at maintaining a specific dollar/yen rate.  \par \par \uc2 GREEN LIGHT  \par \par \uc2 The euro extended gains to $1.1860, less than a cent away from record highs scaled in May and June before a bout of profit-taking pushed it back to session opening levels around $1.1820.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone policymakers continued to sound relaxed about the euro's recent rise.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governing council member Ernst Welteke noted the euro's current rate against the dollar was in line with its long term average, while fellow member Matti Vanhala said euro strength was not a significant hindrance to euro zone growth.  \par \par \uc2 Comments this week by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Wim Duisenberg that the huge U.S. current account deficit made a weaker dollar inevitable fuelled a dollar downtrend that started after Group of Seven finance ministers called for flexible exchange rate regimes last month.  \par \par \uc2 Although Japanese officials were thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars twice on Thursday, their resolve to keep it in check was being tested by a market emboldened by an apparent laissez-faire stance by those overseeing other major economies.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a general consensus that the euro is going to go higher and the ECB is not going to do anything to stop it going higher," said Tim Fox, market strategist at National Australia Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is taking little notice of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Figures showing a surprise fall in German unemployment fuelled optimism that recent labour market reforms were having an effect, but analysts said data out of the euro zone was currently having little impact on the foreign exchanges.  \par \par \uc2 BROAD-BASED FALL  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell to five-year lows against the Swedish crown, six-year lows against the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar and five-year lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Sterling was broadly steady ahead of the Bank of England's monetary policy statement at 1100 GMT. The Bank is widely expected to leave interest rates unchanged at a 48-year low of 3.50 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Questions about the depth of a U.S. recovery centre on strength in the labour market, and weekly jobless claims at 1230 GMT are forecast to show 393,000 new filings, compared with 399,000 in the previous week.  \par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the U.S. Senate Banking Committee on Wednesday confirmed that Treasury Secretary John Snow's testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been delayed so the panel can consider an overhaul of mortgage finance regulation.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031009dza9001vs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
