\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar battered, market wary of BOJ yen sales.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2003\par 10:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The dollar plumbed three-year lows against the yen and 3-1/2 month lows versus the euro on Thursday on growing views the U.S. and European authorities would let it weaken to correct a ballooning U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Although Japanese officials were thought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars twice on Thursday, their resolve to keep it in check was being tested by a market emboldened by an apparent laissez-faire stance by those overseeing other major economies.  \par \par \uc2 Comments this week by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Wim Duisenberg that the huge U.S. current account deficit made a weaker dollar inevitable fuelled a dollar downtrend that started after Group of Seven finance ministers called for flexible exchange rate regimes last month.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a general consensus that the euro is going to go higher and the ECB is not going to do anything to stop it going higher," said Tim Fox, market strategist at National Australia Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is taking little notice of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened to three-year lows of 108.88 yen half a percent down on the day, but recovered to 109.10 by 0735 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar briefly spiked up against the yen in Asian trade and again following a break below 109 in European trade in what dealers said might be Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) officials were not immediately available to confirm whether they had stepped into the market on either occasion.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar went below the figure but then bounced back. Price action would suggest official action but I cannot confirm this," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi of the latest small dollar bounce.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose as far as $1.1860, its highest level since setting record highs above $1.1930 in June.  \par \par \uc2 German unemployment adjusted for seasonal factors fell 14,000 in September to 4.392 million, the Federal Labour Office said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell to five-year lows against the Swedish crown, six-year lows against the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar and five-year lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It hit 9-1/2 year lows against the Canadian dollar on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling, however, hovered below recent three-month highs against the dollar ahead of the Bank of England's monetary policy statement at 1100 GMT, expected to result in no change to UK rates of 3.50 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Questions about the depth of a U.S. recovery centre on strength in the labour market, and weekly jobless claims at 1230 GMT are forecast to show 393,000 new filings, compared with 399,000 in the previous week.  \par \par \uc2 STRONG DOLLAR POLICY  \par \par \uc2 The White House said on Wednesday that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was still that of a strong dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said the mantra rang hollow, particularly after recent remarks by President George W. Bush that he wanted other countries to adopt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy that offered a "level playing field" for American companies.  \par \par \uc2 Combined with Duisenberg's comments, Bush's words were taken as a signal for traders to sell the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 European policymakers continued to show a relaxed stance towards the dollar's decline on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member Matti Vanhala said euro strength was not a significant hindrance to euro zone growth, while ECB member and Belgian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Guy Quaden was quoted in a newspaper as saying flexibility in exchange rates was "favourable".  \par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the U.S. Senate Banking Committee on Wednesday confirmed that Treasury Secretary John Snow's testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been delayed so the panel can consider an overhaul of mortgage finance regulation.  \par \par \uc2 Policies aside, fund flows were pointing to continued yen strength.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data on Thursday showed that foreigners were net buyers of Japanese equities to the tune of 1.0 trillion yen in September, down from 1.6 trillion yen in August but still huge.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031009dza90017x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
