\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar skids as U.S. current account woes persist.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2003\par 18:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The dollar trudged lower against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday amid a growing belief the greenback will have to weaken to narrow the U.S. current account deficit and that a fall has implicit official sanction, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "One thing is pretty clear. We're back to talking about the current account deficit," said Philip Capone, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Fortis Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn., said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is at an "inflection point" where the focus is less on economic growth than on the U.S. current account, a broad measure of a nation's global trade.  \par \par \uc2 Traders remained on the lookout for yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Japanese officials continued their jawboning overnight against the yen's rapid movements.  \par \par \uc2 By midday in U.S. trade, the euro was up 0.22 percent against the dollar at $1.1792, after rising to within one cent of its record high earlier in the session. But the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded nearly flat against the yen on the day, buying about 129.13 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was once again trading below 1.32 francs, off 0.16 percent. The pound was also nearly flat against the dollar at $1.6611.  \par \par \uc2 Gilmore said there is broad acceptance in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that both the United States and Europe are resigned to a weaker dollar. "I think there is broad recognition in the market that there is not much to the U.S. government's strong dollar policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, however, the White House said it is still supporting a strong dollar despite recent comments by both European and U.S. officials that traders have viewed as an attempt to encourage a fall in the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Our policy has always been one of a strong dollar policy," White House spokesman Scott McClellan told reporters in response to a question.  \par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN COMMENTS STILL BOOSTING EURO  \par \par \uc2 But comments from European officials this week led by outgoing European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg that a dollar fall was "unavoidable" have encouraged traders to probe levels for the euro above $1.18. Traders said the euro seems to be a one-way bet against the dollar and as long as short-term moves above $1.17 hold, the uptrend remains in place.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were also nervously awaiting U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow's appearance at a Senate hearing on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies next week, and a summit meeting of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum in Bangkok later this month.  \par \par \uc2 STILL ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH  \par \par \uc2 Traders remained alert for any possible BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following more yen-related comments from Japanese officials overnight.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell below the key 110 yen level on Tuesday but climbed briefly back above 110 amid suspicions \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the greenback. On Wednesday, the dollar fell 0.45 percent to 109.42 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Markets are still anticipating any BoJ action for as long as we're below that 110 yen level and after statements from Japan overnight," said Larry Brickman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banc of America Securities in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Fierce yen-weakening rhetoric ensued in Asian trading, with Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki indicating that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on sharp yen moves.  \par \par \uc2 This was followed by the Finance Ministry's international affairs chief Zembei Mizoguchi, who continued a verbal battle against post-G7 dollar bearishness, saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had tacit approval from other G7 nations.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031008dza800320\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
