\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls on renewed doubts about U.S. recovery.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 15:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 7 (Reuters) - The dollar slumped on Tuesday amid scepticism over the pace of the U.S. economic recovery and additional statements from European officials saying the euro's rise against the greenback is not currently a problem.  \par \par \uc2 In the absence of key U.S. economic data, traders remained on high alert for possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen as the dollar fell to fresh three-year lows against the yen under the 110 level.  \par \par \uc2 In early U.S. trading, the euro was up 0.63 percent against the dollar at $1.1779, rising to a three-month high earlier in the session. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains supported it against the yen, buying about 129.70 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar fell below 1.32 francs, to shed 0.42 percent on the day. The pound rose 0.16 percent to stand above $1.67.  \par \par \uc2 "The overall macroeconomic picture is coming into play," said Tim Mazanec, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Investors bank and Trust Company in Boston. "Worries about the U.S. current account deficit are coming back and foreign capital is just not in place to finance the gap," he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players continued to have lingering doubts over whether Friday's robust labor numbers were convincing enough to signal a reversal in massive U.S. job losses over the last two years.  \par \par \uc2 MORE JAWBONING FROM EUROPE  \par \par \uc2 Additional comments from European officials further added to the dollar's negative tone. "A lot of the dollar's weakness has been due to jawboning from Europe - that they are not complaining about the euro's rise," said Lauren Germain, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America Securities in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Dutch, Belgian and Austrian finance ministers added to the impression that euro zone policymakers were unlikely to oppose the dollar's fall against the euro at this stage, saying the euro's rate was not a concern for the euro zone for now.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, outgoing European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg had indicated that the dollar's decline was "unavoidable" and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to sell euros to halt its rise.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar suffered a late New York sell-off after Duisenberg's comments. Its losses mounted on Tuesday, bringing its fall against the euro to around 2 percent in 24 hours.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH  \par \par \uc2 Markets remained cautious about possible BoJ action to weaken the yen against the dollar after it fell to a new three-year low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 110 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems like there is at least a suspicion of covert support (for the dollar against the yen). Whether there is actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  I am not sure," said Thomas Molloy, a trader at Bank Leumi in New York, adding that he had not seen evidence of it.  \par \par \uc2 "If we do skid (decisively) below 110.0 yen, most of the stops (stop loss orders) will be triggered," which could send the dollar climbing sharply higher, Molloy said.  \par \par \uc2 Mazanec of Investors Bank believes the BoJ may not come in just yet, noting that the dollar's decline against the yen has been orderly so far.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has been actively curbing yen appreciation against the dollar, including one bout of yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted through the New York Federal Reserve last week. (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York and Burton Frierson in London).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031007dza700268\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
