\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones News Highlights:Top Stories Of The Day  \b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par BSKYB SELLS MAN UTD STAKE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 British Sky Broadcasting sells stake in English Premier League soccer club Manchester United for 239 pence a share. Prior to the sale, BSkyB held 25,950,827 Manchester United shares.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALL QUIET ON M&S' HOME FRONT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Marks & Spencer U.K. like-for-like sales for the 11-week period to Sept. 27 up 0.6%, actual sales up 2.6%. But within Home arm, furniture sales decline.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CARLTON, GRANADA MERGER DECISION   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. government expected to announce decision on merger of broadcasters Carlton Communications and Granada Tuesday morning. Secretary of Trade and Industry will rule on proposed merger, initially announced a year ago.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RAFFARIN SAYS FRANCE ON BRINK OF RECESSION   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French Prime Minister estimates France is on the brink of recession, according to press reports quoting him during a trip to Russia. Comments come two days before national statistics institute due to release GDP forecasts for 3Q and 4Q.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIR FRANCE SEES SECTOR GROWTH   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airline industry to eventually grow again by 4% to 5% a year, predicts French carrier's CEO. Also says KLM merger appears acceptable to E.U. Commission and if approved is expected to create EUR450 million in synergies after five years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MMO2 TO DELIVER CHART SONGS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BT's former mobile arm, plans to sell chart music downloads for mobile phones, following a deal with five of music industry's leading labels, according to press reports. Sign of changing attitudes among music publishers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CGD OFFERS ABC EUR1B FOR ATLANTICO   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned Caixa Geral de Depositos bids for Araba Banking Corp's 68.5% stake in Spain's Banco Atlantico, however the offer is lower than the EUR1.1 billion ABC reportedly wants.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS NATIONAL BACK IN PROFIT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Insurer reports 1H profit of CHF16.4 million compared to a loss of CHF36.4 last year on more cautious underwriting.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EASYJET PASSENGERS EXCEED 20M   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 2003 passengers total 1,891,184, an on-year increase of 18.6%. Passengers in rolling 12 months ending Sept. 30 total 20,332,973.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRANCE, EU TONE DOWN ROW   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E.U. authorities tone down budget deficit debate, setting stage for possible face-saving compromise. French Finance Minister says plans low spending, increased taxes to bring deficit below the 3% E.U. limit in 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEORGE WIMPEY SALES STRONG   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Says since release of interim results, U.K. and U.S. housing markets have stayed healthy, and sales rates strong. Targets six new option centers across U.K \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by end of 2004. Also announces CEO to retire at end of 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MATALAN SEES STRONGER 2H   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reports profit before tax of GBP41.2 million for the 6 months to Aug. 31, down from GBP53.6 million last year. Chairman says results "disappointing".  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEORG FISCHER RESTRUCTURES   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss engineering company to begin a restructuring program to boost operating profit by CHF100 million in 2005 and launch a convertible bond to strengthen its capital base. Program will result in the reduction of 1,000 jobs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  MICHAEL PAGE STRONG OVERSEAS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recruiter's 3Q gross profit up to GBP45 million, slightly down from GBP47.8 million in 2002. CEO says U.K, Asia Pacific, U.S. arms all performed well and matched revenues in the previous quarter.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COMMITTED TO YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minster Sadakazu Tanigaki underscores Tokyo's commitment to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to smooth excessive fluctuations, a practice which he said has the backing of the international community. Country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves hit a record high of $604.87 billion in September reflecting the already massive amount of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NTT TO ISSUE Y1 TRILLION IN BONDS   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Nippon Telegraph & Telephone Corp. files a shelf registration at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to issue up to Y1 trillion of corporate bonds in a two-year period starting Oct. 14.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN RECOVERY ON TRACK   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Index of leading economic indicators stood at 55.6 in August, above the boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0 for the fourth straight month. Although the reading marks a slight pullback the economy still remains on a recovery track.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACM THREATENS AHOLD   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amstel Capital Management, which manages 2.5 million in bonds for Ahold's subsidiary Albert Heijn, threatens legal action if the company fails to publicly disclose terms of the 2.6 billion emergency credit line it received in February.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOTAL, ROSNEF IN BLACK SEA JV   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French giant confirms it has agreed to a 50-50 joint venture with the Russian state-owned oil company to explore a deep offshore section in the Black Sea. The agreement is part of Total's strategy to expand in Russia.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ERICSSON KEEPS SONY STAKE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Isn't targeting any acquisitions or disposals and plans to hold on to its 50% stake in mobile telephone joint venture Sony Ericsson. CEO expects growth over the next five years to come from third-generation technology.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANALYSIS: \par  \par EUROPEAN INVESTORS EYE CREDIT MARKET REFORM   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Twenty-six investment management firms join forces to demand sturdier protection in European and U.K. corporate bond market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EDF TUSSLES WITH LEGACY AS IT GOES PRIVATE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After five decades as key state-run instrument in French economy, EdF under pressure to become an ordinary publicly-traded company. But as management aims to show company follows corporate practices, some remain attached to old-fashioned EdF.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FTSE     4255.10    -0.35% \par DAX      3364.77    -1.18% \par CAC      3252.97    -0.87% \par STOXX    2473.10    -0.96% \par DJIA     9594.98    +0.24% \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031007dza7000cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
