\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones News Highlights:Top Stories Of The Day  \b0\par\par\uc2 900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par ALL QUIET ON M&S' HOME FRONT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Marks & Spencer U.K. like-for-like sales for the 11-week period to Sept. 27 up 0.6%, actual sales up 2.6%. But within Home arm, furniture sales decline.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RAFFARIN SAYS FRANCE ON BRINK OF RECESSION   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French Prime Minister estimates France is on the brink of recession, according to press reports quoting him during a trip to Russia. Comments come two days before national statistics institute due to release GDP forecasts for 3Q and 4Q.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CGD OFFERS ABC EUR1B FOR ATLANTICO   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned Caixa Geral de Depositos bids for Araba Banking Corp's 68.5% stake in Spain's Banco Atlantico, however the offer is lower than the EUR1.1 billion ABC reportedly wants.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS NATIONAL BACK IN PROFIT   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Insurer reports 1H profit of CHF16.4 million compared to a loss of CHF36.4 last year on more cautious underwriting.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EASYJET PASSENGERS EXCEED 20M   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 2003 passengers total 1,891,184, an on-year increase of 18.6%. Passengers in rolling 12 months ending Sept. 30 total 20,332,973.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRANCE, EU TONE DOWN ROW   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E.U. authorities tone down budget deficit debate, setting stage for possible face-saving compromise. French Finance Minister says plans low spending, increased taxes to bring deficit below the 3% E.U. limit in 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIR FRANCE SEES SECTOR GROWTH   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airline industry to eventually grow again by 4% to 5% a year, predicts French carrier's CEO. Also says KLM merger appears acceptable to E.U. Commission and if approved is expected to create EUR450 million in synergies after five years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEORGE WIMPEY SALES STRONG   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Says since release of interim results, U.K. and U.S. housing markets have stayed healthy, and sales rates strong. Targets six new option centers across U.K \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by end of 2004. Also announces CEO to retire at end of 2003.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MMO2 TO DELIVER CHART SONGS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BT's former mobile arm, plans to sell chart music downloads for mobile phones, following a deal with five of music industry's leading labels, according to press reports. Sign of changing attitudes among music publishers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SYRIA TO FURTHER CONDEMN ISRAEL   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Country may amend its resolution that seeks U.N. condemnation for the Israeli air strikes on its soil. U.S. renews its warning that it might block any resolution that did not condemn the suicide bombing in Haifa.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOTOROLA'S CHIP UNIT MAY NOT BE BETTER OFF   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While shares climb 10% on news that the handset maker will spin off its chip business, analysts and investors question whether a standalone semiconductor company will be successful given it has underperformed its peers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIVENDI TV UNIT EYED BY PRIVATE FIRMS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French and U.S. private equity firms are looking into Vivendi's NC Numericable, sources say. French media giant has put unit, which has 16% of French cable market, back on market after several previous attempts to sell it.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COMMITTED TO YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minster Sadakazu Tanigaki underscores Tokyo's commitment to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to smooth excessive fluctuations, a practice which he said has the backing of the international community. Country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves hit a record high of $604.87 billion in September reflecting the already massive amount of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NTT TO ISSUE Y1 TRILLION IN BONDS   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Nippon Telegraph & Telephone Corp. files a shelf registration at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to issue up to Y1 trillion of corporate bonds in a two-year period starting Oct. 14.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN RECOVERY ON TRACK   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Index of leading economic indicators stood at 55.6 in August, above the boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0 for the fourth straight month. Although the reading marks a slight pullback the economy still remains on a recovery track.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MICROSOFT RULING SEES CHANGES   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Company set to make "modest changes" to its Windows and Internet Explorer by early 2004 to eliminate computer codes that according to a jury verdict infringe on a patent for launching programs from a Web page using a browser.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GEORG FISCHER RESTRUCTURES   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss engineering company to begin a restructuring program to boost operating profit by CHF100 million in 2005 and launch a convertible bond to strengthen its capital base. Program will result in the reduction of 1,000 jobs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  MICHAEL PAGE STRONG OVERSEAS   \f28 \par \