\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Watch: Policy Likely Steady Friday Despite Yen Gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Hiroshi Inoue \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--While some economists expect the Bank of Japan to address recent yen strength by boosting liquidity, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board will likely keep policy steady when it meets this week due to clear signs Japan's economy remains on a recovery track.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 More liquidity would accommodate further yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise and help offset the harm caused to the economy by the yen's surge.  \par \par \uc2 But arguing against a further easing is a steady flow of strong economic data, including the BOJ's own quarterly tankan survey of business sentiment issued a week ago.  \par \par \uc2 Rather than ease policy at their two-day meeting starting Thursday, the nine-member board will likely endorse an upgrade of the BOJ's assessment of the economy in its next monthly report, due Oct. 14.  \par \par \uc2 The board will also likely finalize a plan announced after its last meeting to broaden the BOJ's market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stabilize interest-rate markets, which have been much more volatile since late June.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ plans to extend maturities of its repurchase agreements on government bonds to one year from six months. It will also begin accepting syndicated loan claims and mortgage-backed securities issued by the Government Housing Loan Corp. as collateral for daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par          Follows 5% Yen Appreciation Vs Dollar \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since the board's previous policy meeting Sept. 11-12, the yen has surged over 5% against the dollar. The greenback fell to a near three-year low against the yen last week of Y110.10 and at 0600 GMT was quoted at Y110.99.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To stem the yen's rise, which threatens to hurt exports and exacerbate deflation, Japan sold a colossal Y4.46 trillion for dollars in September.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some economists say the BOJ could raise its liquidity target, which currently stands at Y27 trillion to Y30 trillion, to mollify the economic impact of a stronger yen and allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue pumping liquidity into the money market while accommodating the flow of yen from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are leaning to the view that the Bank may well surprise the market by raising the current account balance to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's effort to prevent further appreciation of the yen," said Lehman Brothers' Tokyo-based economists in a research note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But those close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  say that the yen hasn't yet reached a level that would spoil Japan's economic recovery.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A rapid rise in the yen is a problematic factor for Japan's economy, but the strong yen hasn't yet hurt the economy or the BOJ's expectations of an economic recovery," said a person close to the BOJ.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, BOJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui last week indicated that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has no intention of implementing further easing steps for the sole purpose of containing the yen's rise.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "When we take things into consideration, we look at the overall economy and do not change our thinking based on one specific factor," Fukui said Friday, according to the nation's major economic newspaper, Nihon Keizai Shimbun.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Strong Tankan To Prompt Upgrade Of Economic View \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts say that while the BOJ board may decide to keep policy steady, a minority of members may call for easier policy in response to the yen's rise.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ will decide to keep monetary policy steady, although one or more members may call for an increase in the account balance target," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The board might discuss increasing the account balance in response to the yen's rise, but will likely agree that such a step isn't as effective as direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said another source close to the BOJ.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Others say the strong tankan survey of business sentiment, while not reflecting the impact of the yen's recent gains as results were collected before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose, will give the board confidence to keep policy steady.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As a result of the tankan survey, the BOJ seems to be more confident of an economic recovery," said Eiji Dohke, chief strategist at UBS Securities Co. "The BOJ is likely to keep monetary policy steady."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The tankan survey showed major manufacturers optimistic about business conditions outnumbered pessimistic firms in September for the first time in 33 months - the second straight quarterly improvement.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The strong tankan survey will encourage the BOJ to upgrade its assessment of the domestic economy and exports, according to those close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The better-than-expected tankan result, including an improvement in sentiment among small- and medium-sized companies, will be incorporated into the economic report," another BOJ source said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In September, the BOJ said economic activity remains "virtually flat", but added that there are signs of improvement in some areas, including exports.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ will likely say this month that there are signs the economy is moving toward recovery.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Hiroshi Inoue, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-9203; hiroshi.inoue@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Hiroshi Inoue, a correspondent for Dow Jones Newswires in Tokyo, has covered the Bank of Japan for a dozen years and also looks at credit markets.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1042 4131  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031007dza70006e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
