\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Continues Fall Vs Yen; New 3-Yr Low Below Y109.50  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jamie McGeever and Tom Barkley  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2003\par 17:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 . NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar spiked above Y110 late Tuesday morning in New York, rising about half a yen in seconds as traders suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese monetary authorities. \u57345\'E0\'01 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had languished earlier in the New York session, dipping to fresh three-year lows at Y109.37 moments before the upward surge. A Japanese bank in New York bought a large amount of dollars to take the dollar back above Y110.00, said a dealer in London, who said it bore all the hallmarks of covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Asked if the buying represented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a source at a Japanese bank in New York said: "I believe so."  \par \par \uc2 At 11:30, however, the dollar had eased back below Y110.00 to Y109.75, sharply lower from Y110.93 late Monday in New York, but up from Y109.37, a level not seen since November 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, the dollar is weaker across the board, as the market's deep bearishness toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows no sign of evaporating.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, more than one Japanese bank was buying dollars in the spike up through Y110.00, dealers said. But all stopped buying above Y110.00, which would suggest the aim of Japanese monetary authorities wasn't to hold the dollar above Y110.00, said dealers.  \par \par \uc2 "If you want to hold it above Y110.00, you'd keep on buying it up to Y110.30, wouldn't you?" said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at a Japanese bank in London. "I think this was a shot across the bows (sending the message) 'We're watching'," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On top of the suspected covert BOJ bids, there are mounting buy orders for dollars from Japanese importers around these levels, say dealers.  \par \par \uc2 But in general, the dollar is weaker across the board Tuesday, and not just against the majors either.  \par \par \uc2 The South African rand surged to a 39-month high of ZAR6.7850 - it was last at that level in July 2000 - before local importer demand for dollars halted its upside momentum.  \par \par \uc2 And the dollar slumped to a seven-year low against the Canadian dollar earlier Tuesday of C$1.3272 before recovering to around C$1.3300 late Tuesday morning.  \par \par \uc2 Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC in New York, said that so far, the effectiveness of the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is open to question.  \par \par \uc2 "If it is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's not causing the dollar bears much pain," he said, saying that would require a push back up through Y110.50. "As long as we stay below Y110.50, that means it's probably headed lower, so it's better to sell into rallies."  \par \par \uc2 The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at the Japanese bank in London agreed.  \par \par \uc2 "We've gone through Y110.00 without a meltdown, but a close in New York (Tuesday) below Y110.00 and it could get nasty," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Around midday in New York, the dollar is zigzagging on both sides of the Y110.00. After Y115.00 was washed away last month, this was the level widely considered to be the new "line in the sand" that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  would defend in order to help maintain the competitiveness of Japanese exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "There's no line in the sand any more," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales in London.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jamie McGeever, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385; tom.barkley@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020031007dza70002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
