\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar retains jobs-led buoyancy,ECB stance mulled.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charlotte Cooper  \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2003\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The dollar touched a one-week high on the euro and recovered versus the yen on Monday, buoyed by a surprise rise in U.S. payrolls last week which fanned hopes for a stronger U.S. recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks were the focus with traders contemplating what was beginning to look like the Bank of Japan's new line in the sand for yen strength at 110.00 yen per dollar and comments from outgoing European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Wim Duisenberg.  \par \par \uc2 The Financial Times said Duisenberg implied in a interview with its Spanish sister paper Expansion that the ECB was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the euro's rise against the dollar. It has gained 10 percent this year versus the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 But a ECB spokesman said Duisenberg did not comment on euro \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interview.  \par \par \uc2 Ryan Shea, senior international economist at Bank One in London said: "It's likely the ECB will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an interest rate cut is more likely, but it is something that will limit the upside for the euro."  \par \par \uc2 "In terms of euro/dollar direction, most of it is still post-payrolls. Many people found Friday's payrolls quite comforting from the point of view that the U.S. economic recovery is probably a bit more sustainable."  \par \par \uc2 By 0740 GMT the dollar stood unchanged on the day at $1.1577 after rising to the one-week high of $1.1533. It hit a three-month low of $1.1768 last week.  \par \par \uc2 It was a quarter of a percent up from late Friday levels against the yen at 111.14 yen but still only one yen away from a three-year low set last week.  \par \par \uc2 ASIA ISSUE  \par \par \uc2 The greenback came under brief pressure in Asia after Jiji new agency, citing financial sources in Beijing, reported that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering revaluing the yuan by nearly 30 percent over the next five years.  \par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations, in a statement on September 20, called for more flexibility on exchange rates, a call the market concluded was aimed at Japan and China in particular.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts were expecting the dollar to hover near current levels against the yen this week since the market might be coming to respect a line in the sand the Japanese authorities drew at 110 yen by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  loudly through the U.S. Federal Reserve last week to support the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's weakness last week was based on speculation about two things - that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be able to aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the G7 communique and that the U.S. was opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley.  \par \par \uc2 "But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stopped the dollar's fall, and they did it through the Fed. Plus we got those payroll figures. So the momentum seems to have abated and I would expect a relatively quiet week ahead."  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, repeated a familiar line on Monday saying the Japanese authorities would take action if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements deviated from fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN ANGLE  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone policy makers say the euro is bearing more than its fair share of the burden of dollar appreciation to adjust the rising U.S. current account gap.  \par \par \uc2 Spanish newspaper Expansion quoted Duisenberg as saying the ECB would do all it can to ensure the dollar's correction was slow and gradual.  \par \par \uc2 "We hope and pray that this adjustment, which is unavoidable, will be slow and gradual. Until now, the adjustment is only against the euro," he said.  \par \par \uc2 German Finance Minister Hans Eichel was quoted in a newspaper saying that the euro zone must be careful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were not too rapid.  \par \par \uc2 Eurozone July retail sales data is due at 1000 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031006dza60012d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
