\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Up Slightly Vs Yen, But Likely Capped  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Twaronite  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2003\par 07:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was a few ticks higher against the yen in Asia Monday, although it gave up most of the day's earlier gains on Japanese sales.  \par \par \uc2 Continued shortcovering after Friday's better-than-expected U.S. jobs data carried the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a high of Y111.19 at 2249 GMT, but profit-taking ensued and accelerated after the pair couldn't manage to stay above Y111, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "There's real demand to sell above Y111.30 from domestic customers so it's not so easy for the dollar to go up sharply," said Tadahiko Nashimoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Barclays Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Many market participants here expect Y110 support to hold this week on perceptions that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from strengthening beyond that level, but many of these same traders are also bearish on the pair over the coming months.  \par \par \uc2 "Y110 is still psychologically and technically a very important level, but overall the longterm picture is still aiming for the dollar at Y105," Nashimoto said. "The good U.S. jobs figures support the scenario that the U.S. is getting better, but it will take more data to confirm it."  \par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance remains unchanged, as a top MOF official reiterated Monday morning.  \par \par \uc2 "When there is overshooting (of moves), and they don't reflect fundamentals, (Japan's) thinking is that we will take the appropriate steps at the right time," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said to reporters.  \par \par \uc2 When Mizoguchi was asked about U.S. President George W. Bush's remarks Friday that "fair trade means \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies that's fair," Mizoguchi said there was no difference in the thinking of Japan, the U.S. and the E.U. on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 Bush's remarks were "common sense - that it's important for the market to reflect fundamentals" in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y110.97, above Y110.85 in New York and Y110.79 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1577, nearly flat from $1.1576 in New York but below $1.1698 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y128.47, compared with Y128.32 in New York and Y129.60 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.6612, compared with $1.6625 in New York and $1.6714 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  aside, market interest centered on a Japanese newswire report that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering revaluing the yuan by nearly 30% within 5 years.  \par \par \uc2 The timeframe mentioned in the Jiji Press report was "reasonable, considering all the problems China has with its banking system," according to one Tokyo-based strategist, who said the report implies China might be trying to appear more flexible about its dollar-pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to avoid the ire of U.S. officials.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S.' evolving attitude about relative \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength will be in sharp focus in the coming weeks, as U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow travels to several U.S. cities to discuss the Bush administration's efforts to strengthen the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Snow will meet U.S. mutual fund industry leaders in Boston on Oct. 9. On Oct. 15, Snow begins a visit to New York, during which he'll meet with Wall Street economists and business leaders and speak at the Conference Board's annual meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "We're very interested in Snow's testimony on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. The whole market is waiting," said Kaneo Ogino, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at HSBC in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031006dza600059\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
