\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady as U.S. payrolls draw near.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 3 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of key U.S. data on Friday, held in check by doubts about a U.S. economic recovery and by caution that Japanese authorities might step in to sell yen for dollars.   \par \par \uc2  The U.S. employment report for September, due at 1230 GMT, is forecast to show a loss of 30,000 jobs in September compared with a loss of 93,000 jobs in August. The unemployment rate is seen at 6.2 percent, up a notch from 6.1 percent.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit three-year lows against the yen earlier this week but recovered some ground as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Tuesday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen.   \par \par \uc2  The dollar also hit three-month lows against the euro this week as investors reassessed their views on the U.S. and global outlook.   \par \par \uc2  "Economists are expecting a negative jobs number today," said Bilal Hafeez, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.   \par \par \uc2  "People jostle for position in the run-up to these numbers, and they are getting more mixed in their views on the U.S. economy, whereas two weeks ago they were more optimistic."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar drifted within half yen of three-year lows around 110.10 yen\par  and just over a half a cent off three-month lows around $1.1770 to the\par euro       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was trading at 110.53 yen and $1.1710 per euro at 0720 GMT, a touch\par below the U.S. close.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was below levels against the yen at which Japanese\par authorities were widely believed to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday,\par following confirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  near 110 on Tuesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The 110 level is seen as the new line in the sand for Japanese\par authorities.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As we near 110 yen, the market naturally gets anxious about possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at JP Morgan\par Chase in Tokyo.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A chorus of Japanese officials, worried that a higher yen could derail\par the country's export-led economic recovery, have been warning on a\par daily basis that volatility in exchange rates was undesirable and Japan\par would act against it as needed.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. JOBS DATA\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The main focus on Friday was the monthly U.S. jobs data, given concerns\par that a soft labour market would eventually take a toll on consumer\par spending, the main driver of the U.S. economic recovery over the\par years.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is waiting for the key U.S. job data, but the view is\par pretty mixed with some worrying about weak figures, and others\par expecting a very positive outcome," said Tanase.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the bearish sentiment on the dollar was widespread and\par even a positive surprise in the non-farm payrolls figures might only\par support the dollar for a very short while.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Also on Friday, the Institute of Supply Management's non-manufacturing\par survey for September is due at 1400 GMT, forecast to have fallen to\par 62.5 from 65.1 but still well above the 50 threshold that indicates\par expansion.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the euro zone, Reuters services purchasing managers index at 0800\par GMT is forecast to show a slight increase to 52.5 in September, from\par the previous 52.0.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile in Tokyo, Japanese Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka said yen\par strength would not have a major impact in the next six to 12 months\par from a macroeconomic standpoint.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031003dza3000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
