\par\par \b \uc2 Bush Says He Is Pressuring Other Countries On  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alex Keto  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2003\par 18:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--President George W. Bush said Friday that he is putting pressure on other countries to make sure their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates don't work to undercut U.S. manufacturers.  \par \par \uc2 In the speech in Milwaukee, Bush didn't single out any countries he is talking to about their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but in the past he has cited both China and Japan as countries that keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  artificially low.  \par \par \uc2 "We've been talking to countries about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, to make sure that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of a government don't disadvantage America. Fair trade means \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies that's fair," Bush said.  \par \par \uc2 "The manufacturing sector is concerned about the playing field being level. This administration will work to level that playing field. We can compete with anybody. We just expect the rules to treat us fairly," Bush added.  \par \par \uc2 In the case of the China, Beijing maintains a policy of pegging its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the yuan at a fixed rate against the dollar. In the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to adjust the price of the yen against the dollar and to keep the yen from rapidly appreciating against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alex Keto, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-9256; Alex.Keto@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031003dza3000qe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
