\par\par \b \uc2 Resurgent yen undeterred by huge BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 22:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The yen has not reversed its appreciating trend against the dollar despite massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this year to weaken the Japanese unit against the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's recent decline against the yen broadly signaled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next major downtrend against other major rivals as well, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Technical charts suggest the yen's underlying bias is still bullish in the short to medium term, said Jordan Kotick, technical analyst at JP Morgan Chase, underpinned by hefty portfolio inflows to Japan.  \par \par \uc2 So most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts are questioning whether the BoJ's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a strategy intended to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade advantage, has been effective at all.  \par \par \uc2 "Certainly, the BoJ's action had immediate effect. But can you build an economic policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? I don't think so," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Connecticut.  \par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that in September alone, the BoJ sold 4.5 trillion yen, or about $40 billion. Analysts say this is roughly equivalent to more than half the total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out in the whole of the first half of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Despite record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for September, the yen appreciated by more than 5 percent against the dollar in the first half of September alone, roughly a week before a meeting of the Group of Seven major industrialized nations in Dubai, according to estimates from Lehman Brothers.  \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought approximately $90 billion worth of dollars and yet the yen strengthened by over 6 percent versus the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 Looking at just the months when there has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, the BoJ has bought an average $22.7 billion per month but the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen by an average 1.8 percent against the dollar each month, Lehman said.  \par \par \uc2 It is likely that the BoJ - which acts on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - did at least limit the yen's export-damaging rise.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts may argue that the yen would probably have risen much further had the BoJ stood aside and done nothing. But Lehman said "considering the amounts that have been spent, the return on the BoJ's investment has been disappointing."  \par \par \uc2 Most U.S.-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists believe the BoJ is facing a losing battle in trying to prevent the dollar from slipping below a certain level against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which at the moment stands at 110 yen, traders agree. A strategy of trying to weaken the yen when most fundamental indicators argue against it will merely succeed in slowing the yen's rise but not reversing it, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the BoJ can hold the dollar/yen to any level," said Gilmore of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics, especially with the way Japan's economy has been performing.  \par \par \uc2 Activity in the world's second biggest economy has recently picked up the pace after a long downturn, surprising some analysts.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza200485\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
