\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pares gains - U.S. jobs jitters weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 19:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The dollar shed its early gains to trade nearly flat against the euro on Thursday as negative sentiment ahead of Friday's monthly U.S. employment report weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, traders continued to fret in the aftermath of suspected yen-weakening Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the global day.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback jumped about half a percent on the yen early in Asia and blipped up again later, with traders reporting Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the dollar retreated near session lows against the yen shortly after noon in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "Until tomorrow's numbers, I think everybody is short dollars," said Ed Stapleton, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Fortis Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Being "short" a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effectively a bet that it will decline.  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters expect U.S. non-farm payroll jobs to have fallen by 30,000 in September and a jobless rate of 6.2 percent. But some market analysts expect a much steeper fall in non-farm payroll jobs, Stapleton said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shortly after noon in New York, the euro  was nearly flat on the day at\par $1.1710. Against the yen       , the dollar was slightly higher, up\par 0.08 percent to 110.65 yen. Against the Swiss franc        the dollar\par was at 1.3146 francs, up 0.08 percent on the day.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pound was up 0.2 percent to $1.6722.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAPAN MOF DECLINES COMMENT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official declined to comment on whether Tokyo had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying it would only disclose its actions immediately if it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through an overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - as it did through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York on Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Then, Japanese authorities sold yen for dollars through the New York Fed in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's first confirmed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since the Group of Seven major industrialized nations called for flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates on Sept. 20. The action sent the dollar sharply higher.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a hot topic" because of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's actions and officials' remarks this week, said Jeremy Fand, senior proprietary trader with WestLB in New York. In addition, speculation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market that the Reserve Bank of Australia might have acted on behalf of Japan in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets "is giving the impression that the MOF is putting more potential tactics in place," Fand said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of Australia in New York declined to comment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sources at Japan's MOF said the ministry was considering expanding the borrowing limit for its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  account - the war chest for its yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - by up to 20 trillion yen ($180.7 billion) from 79 trillion yen currently.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the Bank of Japan strongly suspected of propping up the dollar against the yen to protect Japanese exporters, dollar bears focused their attention on the euro instead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "When we get \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dollar bears tend to vent their bearishness on freely-floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like euro and sterling," said Aziz McMahon, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (James Thornhill in London contributed to this report).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2003wt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
