\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar advances as traders mull Japan's tactics.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, changes dateline, previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The dollar recovered from three-month lows against the euro and was higher against some other major rivals on Thursday as traders continued to fret about suspected yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The greenback jumped about a half a percent on the yen early in Asia, and blipped up again later, with traders reporting Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar was hovering around the 111 yen level in jittery early morning trade in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Early morning in New York, the euro was down 0.4 percent on the day to $1.1669. Against the yen, the dollar was up 0.4 percent to 110.96 yen. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3206 francs, up 0.5 percent on the day.  \par \par \uc2 The pound was up 0.04 percent to $1.6683.  \par \par \uc2 A senior Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official declined to comment on whether Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it would only disclose its actions immediately if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as it did through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Japanese authorities sold yen for dollars through the New York Fed in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Group of Seven major industrialized nations called for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on Sept. 20. The action sent the dollar sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a hot topic" because of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions and officials' remarks this week said Jeremy Fand, senior proprietary trader with WestLB in New York. In addition, speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that the Reserve Bank of Australia might have acted on behalf of Japan in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "is giving the impression that the MOF is putting more potential tactics in place," Fand said.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of Australia in New York declined to comment.  \par \par \uc2 Sources at Japan's MOF said the ministry was considering expanding the borrowing limit for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account - the war chest for its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - by up to 20 trillion yen ($180.7 billion) from 79 trillion yen currently.  \par \par \uc2 With the Bank of Japan strongly suspected of propping up the dollar against the yen to protect Japanese exporters, dollar bears focused their attention on the euro instead.  \par \par \uc2 "When we get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar bears tend to vent their bearishness on freely-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like euro and sterling," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 DUISENBERG: NO EXCHANGE RATE IN MIND  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its minimum bid rate unchanged at 2.0 percent, in a widely expected decision.  \par \par \uc2 The euro scraped session lows shortly after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said in a press conference the ECB has no exchange rate for the euro in mind which it would call appropriate and that day-to-day \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements do not influence ECB decisions.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar mainly shrugged aside U.S. economic data, although traders are starting to brace for the U.S. monthly employment report due on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 First-time filings for state jobless benefits climbed 13,000 to 399,000 in the week ended Sept. 27, the Labor Department said on Thursday, slightly higher than the 395,000 expected by analysts. The dollar hardly wobbled. (James Thornhill in London contributed to this report).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2003id\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
