\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar soft pre-jobs data, BOJ seen helping vs yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By James Thornhill  \par \uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The dollar eased to three-month lows versus the euro on Thursday as worries over the strength of the U.S. recovery returned ahead of key labour market data, but found support against the yen from suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A weaker-than-expected U.S. manufacturing report on Wednesday added to a recent string of soft data out of the world's biggest economy, fanning concerns an economic upturn might not be as powerful as expected.  \par \par \uc2 A two-percent jump on Wall Street on Wednesday failed to give support to the greenback in a market which is concerned that U.S. weekly jobless claims data later on and Friday's payroll report could generate further downward pressure.  \par \par \uc2 With the Bank of Japan (BOJ) strongly suspected of propping up the dollar against the yen to protect local exporters, dollar bears focused their attentions on the euro instead.  \par \par \uc2 "When we get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar bears tend to vent their bearishness on freely-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like euro and sterling," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "Last week's (U.S.) claims number was affected by Hurricane Isabel, so we should get a better idea from today's data...People use an average of claims to project what payrolls will be," he added.  \par \par \uc2 By 0945 GMT, the dollar traded at $1.1715 per euro broadly steady from late New York levels, though off an earlier low of $1.1768. The euro was also up nearly half a percent against the yen at 129.90 (EURJPY=).  \par \par \uc2 The greenback jumped about a half a percent on the yen early in Asia, and blipped up again later, with traders reporting BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but drifted back under the 111 level in Europe .  \par \par \uc2 A senior Finance Ministry official declined to comment on whether Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not, saying it would only disclose its actions immediately if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as it did through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. JOBS DATA EYED  \par \par \uc2 Investors are worried about a possible rise in U.S. weekly jobless claims especially as this week's economic indicators all point to a soft payrolls report on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Initial claims are expected to rise to 395,000 in the week ended September 27 from 381,000 the previous week, when this number contracted to its lowest since early February.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Institute for Supply Management index of manufacturing activity slipped to 53.7 from 54.7 in August, falling short of a consensus forecast.  \par \par \uc2 "Investor faith in the U.S. recovery story has taken a fairly pronounced knock, which you can seen in the dollar's value," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro's nearly 10 big figure jump (since September) is partly because of Japanese investor appetite for euro zone government debt. The risk reward is also shifting in favour of a flat dollar position from overweight."  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces its rate decision at 1145 GMT in Lisbon but no-one expects a policy shift and analysts are more closely focused on the monthly news conference that follows at 1230 GMT and possible comments on euro strength.  \par \par \uc2 "The ECB's top priority is \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. If your goal is price stability you don't want big moves up or down," said McMahon at ABN.  \par \par \uc2 WAR CHEST  \par \par \uc2 Inflows into Japan showed some signs of abating with MOF data showing foreign investors had turned net sellers of Japanese stocks last week.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said that was likely to be a temporary move related to the end of the quarter and sentiment was even more positive given Wednesday's upbeat "tankan" business survey from the BOJ and a resumption of a bull run in Tokyo stocks .  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei stock average ended up 2.24 percent.  \par \par \uc2 To counter such flows and curb any export-damaging yen rise, Japan conducted a record 13.5 trillion yen of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of this year.  \par \par \uc2 Sources at the MOF said the ministry was considering expanding the borrowing limit for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account - the war chest for its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - by up to 20 trillion yen ($180.7 billion) from 79 trillion yen currently.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2002ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
