\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar under pressure despite blips vs yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shinichi Kishima  \par \uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to three-month lows against the euro and struggled to hold gains made versus the yen on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities on Thursday amid persistent worries about the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Although the dollar jumped about a half percent against the yen in early trade, and blipped up again later, on what traders said was yen-selling by Japan to contain the recent sharp rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the gains quickly dissipated.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at lower levels and cause knee-jerk reactions, fresh selling comes in once the rise stalls," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the interbank desk at Trust & Custody Services Bank.  \par \par \uc2 A senior Finance Ministry official declined to comment on whether Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not, saying it would only disclose its actions immediately if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through an overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as it did on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, was seen as a sign that the U.S. authorities were giving a tacit approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , tempering yen bullishness somewhat.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the dollar remains within one percent of three-year lows around 110.10 yen set this week. At 0548 GMT, it stood at 110.95 yen up from 110.60 yen late on Wednesday but down from the day's peak around 111.30 yen touched after the early spike-up.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone by now knows what the Japanese authorities' stance is," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Sumitomo Life Insurance. "The question is whether they get support from the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 "Until the U.S. explicitly expresses its support for Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the market will be skeptical about a sustained upturn in the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters blocking the dollar's down moves against the yen, the euro was the main beneficiary of growing interest in selling dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose above $1.1765 up about half a cent on the day and about 10 cents over the past month. Traders said June peaks of around $1.1930, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest level since its birth in 1999, were now back in sight.  \par \par \uc2 Despite a two-percent rally in the Dow Jones industrial average, traders said recent data suggesting a soft labour market were raising concerns about an eventual impact on personal consumption, the main engine of U.S. economic expansion.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the focus was on Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls figures.  \par \par \uc2 WAR CHEST  \par \par \uc2 The yen was supported by Wednesday's upbeat "tankan" business survey from the Bank of Japan and a resumption of a bull run in the Nikkei share price average, which were likely to keep luring in foreign investment flows.  \par \par \uc2 MOF data showed that foreign investors had turned net sellers of Japanese stocks last week, but traders said that was likely to be a temporary move related to the end of the quarter.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei has begun the new quarter on a strong note, rising 2.24 percent by the end of trade to add to Wednesday's gains.  \par \par \uc2 Without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen would likely continue to face strong upward pressure in the near term, traders said. Sources at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the ministry was considering expanding the borrowing limit for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account - the war chest for its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - by up to 20 trillion yen ($180.7 billion) from 79 trillion yen currently.  \par \par \uc2 Japan conducted a record 13.5 trillion yen of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of this year, leaving about 12 trillion yen or so under the current ceiling. ($1=110.67 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
