\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar jumps vs yen but broadly under pressure.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shinichi Kishima  \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2003\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the yen on Thursday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities but was otherwise broadly weak, dipping to three-month lows against the euro on worries about the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Even the gains on the yen began to dissipate soon after the dollar spiked up half a percent, underlining the underlying weakness of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at lower levels and cause knee-jerk reactions, fresh selling comes in once the rise stalls," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of the interbank desk at Trust & Custody Services Bank.  \par \par \uc2 A senior Finance Ministry official declined to comment on whether Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not, saying it would only disclose its actions immediately if it interevened through an overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as it did on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, was seen as a sign that the U.S. authorities were giving a tacit approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tempered yen bullishness somewhat.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the dollar remains within sight of three-year lows around 110.10 yen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0225 GMT, it stood at around 110.95 yen up from around 110.60 yen late on Wednesday but down from the day's peak of around 111.30 yen set after the early spike-up.  \par \par \uc2 The euro rose to three-month highs above $1.1760 up a quarter cent on the day, amid worries about the health of the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Despite a two-percent rally in the Dow Jones industrial average, traders said recent data suggesting a soft labour market were raising concerns about an eventual impact on personal consumption, the main engine of U.S. economic expansion.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the focus was on Friday's non-farm payrolls figures.  \par \par \uc2 NIKKEI RALLY  \par \par \uc2 The yen was supported by Wednesday's upbeat "tankan" business survey from the Bank of Japan and a resumption of a bull run in the Nikkei share price average, which were likely to keep luring in foreign investment flows.  \par \par \uc2 MOF data showed that foreign investors had turned net sellers of Japanese stocks last week, but traders said that was likely to be a temporary move related to the end of the quarter.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei has begun the new quarter on a strong note, rising 1.18 percent by midday on Thursday to add to Wednesday's gains.  \par \par \uc2 Without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen would likely continue to face strong upward pressure in the near term, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "Although the autallowed the dollar to fall below 110," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of the bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Daiwa Securities SMBC. The Nihon Keizai Shimbun financial daily reported that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) was considering expanding the borrowing limit for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account - the war chest for its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - by up to 20 trillion yen ($180.7 billion) from 79 trillion yen currently.  \par \par \uc2 Japan conducted a record 13.5 trillion yen of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first nine months of this year, leaving about 12 trillion yen or so under the current ceiling. The MOF wanted to act before a dwindling war chest invites speculators to step up their yen buying, the newspaper said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031002dza2000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
