\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  aims to up  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  borrowing cap-Nikkei.  \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 22:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 1 (Reuters) - One day after Japan stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with a hefty round of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to raise its borrowing limits for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Underscoring its commitment to stem excessive appreciation of the yen, the MOF is considering raising the ceiling on government borrowing to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by 10-20 trillion yen (up to $180 billion) from the current 79 trillion yen ($712 billion), the Nikkei reported on its online news site.  \par \par \uc2 With yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government already running to more than 10 trillion ($90 billion) so far this fiscal year. The Nikkei story said: "Concerns are emerging that the nation's monetary authorities could run into the borrowing ceiling,"  \par \par \uc2 Nikkei reported that as a result, the MOF has concluded that it is necessary to raise the borrowing limit to head off potential speculation in the market that it may be running out of financial resources to keep a lid on upward yen pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Such financing is obtained via the issuance of yen-denominated short term government debt securities, while the maximum limit on such borrowing is approved by Japan's Diet as part of the central government's budget.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday Japanese authorities sold yen for dollars through the Federal Reserve Bank of New York in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Group of Seven nations called for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on Sept. 20. The action sent the dollar sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 Some New York-based analysts estimated the size of Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at between $8 billion and $10 billion.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Wayne Cole).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031001dza100308\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
