\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  trade up 15-30 pct when BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  Tuesday.   \b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 18:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trade surged by between 15 and 30 percent on Tuesday as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen, settlement bank CLS and news and information company Reuters (RTR.L) said.   \par \par \uc2 The number of contracts on Reuters' spot matching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing system hit its highest level since 1996, Reuters said, although it declined to give an absolute figure.   \par \par \uc2 "On Tuesday we were up about 30 percent on an average day. Dollar/yen volume was double an average day," a Reuters spokeswoman said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar had a huge two yen reversal of fortune when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the New York Federal Reserve to pull the yen back from three-year highs against the battered U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Frenetic trading saw the dollar surge higher in a matter of minutes against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the euro, sterling and the Australian dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The spokeswoman said Reuters' system also saw an exceptional number of trades in the Australian dollar and sterling against the U.S. dollar and in euro/sterling, euro/Swedish crown and euro/Norwegian crown.   \par \par \uc2 Trade on Reuters' conversational dealing system was also up on Tuesday but no figures were available.   \par \par \uc2 The global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is estimated to turn over a net $1.2 trillion a day and CLS, the global settlement bank, said preliminary data from its system showed Tuesday's volume on course to be around 15 percent higher than an average day.   \par \par \uc2 "CLS has seen an increase in volume and value terms for both the Tuesday and Wednesday settlement cycles," said Jonathan Butterfield, CLS executive vice president of marketing and communication.   \par \par \uc2 "We've had a 15 percent higher number of contracts processed for both days than our current running average."   \par \par \uc2 There was also suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian trade on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 CLS, which went live a year ago, provides a live link between \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlement systems.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently settled on the system are the U.S., Australian, Canadian and Singapore dollars, the euro, yen, sterling and Swiss franc and the Danish, Norwegian and Swedish crowns.   \par \par \uc2 No one could be reached for comment about volumes at electronic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker EBS.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031001dza1002jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
