\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar near day's low vs yen,BOJ effect shortlived.  \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 08:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 1 (Reuters) - The dollar held one yen above the previous day's three-year low in early European trade on Wednesday, helped by market suspicions of a fresh bout of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the yen lower.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo dealers reported possible Bank of Japan bids behind a jump up in the dollar from 111.05 yen to 111.40 late in Asian trade but it quickly slipped back to 111.17.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dollar/yen through the New York Federal Reserve in late European trade, action which drove the dollar up from lows around 110.07.  \par \par \uc2 BOJ Governor Fukui said stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were essential for Japan to beat deflation and the Bank was watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and long term rates closely.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's quarterly "tankan" business survey hit an upbeat note, with the key diffusion index rising to plus one, from minus five three months earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was holding half a cent below the previous day's three-month high of $1.1737 , just two cents off its record peaks hit in May and June.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing is due to speak in Zurich at 0730 GMT and euro zone purchasing managers indices for September are due between 0745-0800 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The pan-euro zone index is forecast at 49.7 from 49.1 in August, still below the 50 level that divides contraction from expansion.   \par \par 