\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-NYMEX crudes in slow retreat after sharp NY rise.   \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 04:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - NYMEX crude oil futures beat a slow retreat in Asia on Wednesday on light corrective selling following steep rises in New York, where trading was driven by bids linked to an expiry of gasoline futures.   \par \par \uc2 The market retained the bullish tone set after OPEC's unexpected decision last week to slash output, but Asian traders were wary of bidding ahead of closely watched U.S. weekly inventory data later in the day.   \par \par \uc2 Sentiment was also helped by news that the Nigeria Labor Congress had called a meeting for October to consider resuming a general strike over fuel prices.   \par \par \uc2 "Prices remain buoyant. There is also a very strong bargain-hunting appetite in the market," said a trader at a Tokyo-based brokerage.   \par \par \uc2 At 0124 GMT, key crude oil futures for November delivery were down eight cents at $29.12 a barrel in electronic ACCESS trade compared with the New York close.   \par \par \uc2 In the previous day, the November contract hit a $29.38, its highest since September 11.   \par \par \uc2 "People are a bit nervous about chasing on rallies due to speculation that U.S. inventories will pick up," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Crude stocks are expected to show a 1.13 million barrel rise while distillate supplies are expected to edge higher by 900,000 barrels, according to a Reuters survey of analysts on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Gasoline stocks are forecast to rise 2.0 million barrels.   \par \par \uc2 "Heading towards winter, the market is paying close attention to stocks of heating oil and distillates," the trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Oil price on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange rose sharply across the board, with sentiment boosted by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day.   \par \par \uc2 Although the yen regained strength after falling as low as around 112 yen against the dollar, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was well-capped by wariness over further action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which made investors keen about buying yen-based oil futures.   \par \par \uc2 Key February crude jumped 370 yen to 17,220 yen per kilolitre from Tuesday's settlement.   \par \par \uc2 April gasoline rose 430 yen to 26,450 yen.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April gas oil  was up 430 yen at 25,130 yen, and kerosene for April\par delivery         350 yen to 24,550.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031001dza10006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
