\par\par \b \uc2 Japan stocks slip despite tankan, Wall St drags.  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2003\par 02:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Japanese shares erased opening gains to fall in early Wednesday trade as an encouraging result in the Bank of Japan's "tankan" survey failed to inspire wideranging buying, reflecting sentiment dimmed by a retreat in U.S. stocks.  \par \par \uc2 Stocks seen having better earnings prospects gained ground, with Mitsubishi Tokyo Financial Group rising 3.69 percent to 731,000 yen.  \par \par \uc2 But shares of several exporters came under pressure after falls on Wall Street following unexpectedly weak reports on business activity in the Midwest and U.S. consumer confidence.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei average was down 0.37 percent or 37.44 points at 10,181.61 as of 0029 GMT after rising as high as 10,262.84 soon after the opening.  \par \par \uc2 The broader TOPIX index was down 0.33 percent at 1,015.47.  \par \par \uc2 Chip and computer maker Hitachi Ltd was down 0.97 percent at 614 yen and Nikon Corp, the world's second-largest maker of steppers, used for producing chips, slumped 2.06 percent to 1,518.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a tug of war between negative factors, including a plunge in U.S. tech stocks, and positive factors such as the BOJ tankan results and a halt in the yen's rise," said Masaharu Sakudo, an adviser at Tachibana Securities.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the current correction mode, however, the market failed to react directly to the positive factors."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's closely watched tankan survey, released before the market opened, produced a key diffusion index of sentiment for large manufacturers of plus 1 in September, beating a forecast of zero in a Reuters poll of economists and improving from minus 5 in June.  \par \par \uc2 The tankan measures business sentiment by comparing the percentage of companies reporting unfavourable conditions from those that say they are favourable.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's rebound against the yen overnight on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken an export-denting rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to grab investors' full attention in slow trade on the first day of the fiscal year's second half.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at around 111.30 yen in early morning trade after leaping on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York from a three-year trough of around 110.07 yen.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031001dza100020\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\ri